; displaywarp.eval - the display list, read apart from the GPU that renders
; (code-review C198, C199, C197). JUDGED by tools\DisplayTest.py, which runs it
; HEADLESS on `-warp` - the software rasterizer, which has no outputs of its own,
; exactly like a hybrid laptop's discrete GPU - and reads each `video status`
; after the line before it:
;
;   boot        the running adapter (WARP) is listed and staged, and the monitor
;               and resolution lists are NOT empty: monitors are every adapter's
;               outputs, not the rendering one's (on a hybrid laptop they were
;               empty, and Borderless did nothing).
;   borderless  `video apply borderless` takes: the window covers the staged
;               monitor's desktop rect (hidden, it is only resized - C391).
;   ghost       a monitor that is not there is put in the list and staged - the
;               list a cable pulled after it was read would hold...
;   change      ...and a WM_DISPLAYCHANGE, posted to the window and taken by the
;               real pump, re-reads the list: the ghost is gone and a real
;               monitor is staged again.
;   ini         the staged monitor's device name and the GPU's identity survive
;               settings.ini's text both ways (written as Save writes, read as
;               Load reads - the text, never the player's file).
;
; Every apply here is a SCRIPT's, so it is applied and never saved. No world is
; needed for any of it; the game is started first only because a script must
; end playing to reach its verdict.
newgame
video status
video apply borderless
video status
video ghost
video status
video displaychange
video status
video ini
video apply windowed 1280x720
video status
